      "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/917273/000119312526431941/rmbs-20260930.htm",
      "excerpt": "Contract and other revenue accounted for 13% and 12% of our consolidated revenue for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, respectively, as compared to 11% for both the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025. 25 Costs and Expenses Cost of product revenue mainly includes costs attributable to the sale of memory interface chip products. Cost of product revenue increased approximately $11.2 million and $21.5 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, respectively, as compared to the same periods in 2025. The increases were primarily due to additional inventory and production costs to support higher sales volumes of our memory interface chips. Cost of contract and other revenue reflects the portion of the total engineering costs that is specifically devoted to individual customer development and support services. Cost of contract and other revenue increased $0.3 million and $1.0 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, respectively, as compared to the same periods in 2025. The increases were primarily due to higher costs of engineering services associated with the contracts. Total research and development expenses for the three months ended September 30, 2026 are consistent with amounts from the same period in 2025, decreasing by approximately $0.1 million. The slight decrease was primarily due to a $1.9 million reduction in prototyping costs, partially offset by increases of $1.2 million in stock-based compensation expenses and $1.0 million in payroll-related expenses. Total research and development expenses for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 increased approximately $12.2 million as compared to the same period in 2025. The increase was primarily driven by continued investment in our research and development initiatives and reflected higher payroll-related expenses of $7.2 million, stock-based compensation expenses of $2.6 million, depreciation expense of $1.8 million and prototyping costs of $0.8 million, partially offset by decreases in other research and development expenses. Total sales, general and administrative expenses for the three months ended September 30, 2026 increased approximately $8.5 million as compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to increases in professional fees of $5.2 million, stock-based compensation expenses of $1.8 million and payroll-related expenses of $1.1 million.",
